{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"artifactsRead\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/04-lifecycle-exercise/ruling-011-response.json\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/quick-fix/004-quick-fix.json\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Follow-up verification focused on SV-04-001 convergence. The impl-lead ruling and story spec now explicitly accept threadId-only normalization for materialized-file equality, and the existing lifecycle tests match that accepted contract. Both configured gates pass.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[{\"id\":\"SV-04-001\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"rationale\":\"Resolved by ruling-011 and the updated story contract. The ruling artifact accepts threadId-normalized materialized-file equality and rejects test-only thread-id injection as a forbidden production shim. The story now defines AC-5.3/TC-5.2 and AC-5.4/TC-5.3 as literal pull equality plus materialized-file equality after substituting only the intentionally random thread id, with differing ids required (`stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md:27-33`, `:123-128`). The lifecycle tests assert that contract: only `threadId` is replaced (`test/lifecycle.test.ts:97-103`), replay ids must differ (`:282-285`), pull equality is literal (`:274-280`), and teardown pull/health plus normalized file equality are checked (`:296-302`).\"}],\"newFindings\":[],\"openFindings\":[],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-5.1 / TC-5.1 full lifecycle operations return ok through deterministic SDK configuration\",\"AC-5.2 / TC-5.1 checkpoint coherence across pull, health, compact receipt, rebuild, and edited/deleted content\",\"AC-5.3 / TC-5.2 literal pull-output equality plus threadId-only normalized materialized-file equality under ruling-011\",\"AC-5.4 / TC-5.3 fresh-SDK teardown continuity with final pull equality, health deep-equality, and threadId-only normalized materialized-file equality under ruling-011\",\"AC-5.5 / TC-5.4 spawned CLI overview/view/messages-list parity at three lifecycle checkpoints\"],\"unverified\":[]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"pass\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"`pnpm verify` passed: 328 tests across 32 files.\",\"`pnpm verify-all` passed: 366 tests across 44 files, including the process suite.\",\"The quick-fix was doc-only; no production runtime path was changed for the ruling.\"]}"}}
